  "question": {
    "text": "Resistance of a wire at $0^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}, 100^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ and $t^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$ is found to be $10 \\Omega, 10.2 \\Omega$ and $10.95 \\Omega$ respectively. The temperature $t$ in Kelvin scale is _________"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "748",
  "solution": {
    "text": "$\\begin{aligned} & \\mathrm{R}=\\mathrm{R}_0(1+\\alpha \\Delta \\mathrm{T}) \\\\ & \\frac{\\Delta \\mathrm{R}}{\\mathrm{R}_0}=\\alpha \\Delta \\mathrm{T}\\end{aligned}$\nCase-I\n$\\begin{aligned} & 0{ }^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C} \\rightarrow 100^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C} \\\\ & \\frac{10.2-10}{10}=\\alpha(100-0)\\end{aligned}$   ...(1)\nCase-II\n$0^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C} \\rightarrow \\mathrm{t}^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C}$\n$\\frac{10.95-10}{10}=\\alpha(\\mathrm{t}-0)$   ...(2)\n$\\begin{aligned} & \\Rightarrow \\frac{\\mathrm{t}}{100}=\\frac{0.95}{0.2}=475^{\\circ} \\mathrm{C} \\\\ & \\mathrm{t}=475+273=748 \\mathrm{~K}\\end{aligned}$"
  }
}